NAME
       clock_gettime, clock_settime, sleep, uptime - time

SYNOPSIS
       #include <time.h>
       #include <unistd.h>

       int clock_gettime(int clk, struct timespec *ts);
       int clock_settime(int clk, const struct timespec *ts);
       int usleep(useconds_t usec);
       unsigned sleep(unsigned seconds);

DESCRIPTION
       CLOCK_REALTIME is wall clock time and can be set; the ntpdate
       command uses that. CLOCK_MONOTONIC counts from boot and never
       jumps, so it is the one to use for measuring intervals.

       Time is served by a cascade that calibrates the local APIC timer
       against the TSC and falls back to APIC ticks on machines with no
       HPET, so these calls work on hardware where the HPET is absent.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EINVAL   the clock id is not known
       EPERM    setting the clock requires root

SEE ALSO
       uptime(1), date(1), ntpdate(1), poll(2)
